{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Hss</b> — in the manner of: ידמו כאבן ('they shall be silent like stone')." "<b>And the word נעור</b> — from the nifal binyan, like נכון, and this binyan comes both in present tense and in past tense, like נכונו ללצים שפטים ('judgments are prepared for scoffers') and הממלכה נכונה ('the kingdom is established') — this too, נעור, is past tense, and the future is אשר יעור משנתו ('when one awakens from his sleep'), and a kamatz katan comes instead of a gadol — perhaps because of the guttural letter. And the commentator who says it is like נערו כגורי אריות ('they were stirred up like lion cubs') holds a correct opinion, because of the word הס."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:47.919078251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}